<title>ITALY: Italy Senate votes to create communications body.</title>
<headline>Italy Senate votes to create communications body.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Senate (upper house) on Wednesday approved the creation of a watchdog authority for the communications sector.</p>
<p>The favourable vote was for the first of four parts of a draft bill proposed by Posts and Telecommunications Minister Antonio Maccanico concerning the television and telecoms sector.</p>
<p>Establishment of the watchdog body is a prerequisite for the privatisation of state telecommunications holding Stet, due to be merged with its operating unit Telecom Italia and sold off later this year.</p>
<p>After Senate approval of the bill it then passes to the lower Chamber of Deputies.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
